er-images/Dockerfile-testcontainers_ryuk), matching the pattern used by the existing microcks-testcontainers test.\",\n      \"applied_setup\": [\n        {\n          \"coordinate\": \"org.testcontainers:testcontainers-couchbase:2.0.5\",\n          \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n          \"result\": \"applied\",\n          \"target\": \"tests/src/org.springframework.data/spring-data-couchbase/6.1.1/build.gradle\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"coordinate\": \"org.testcontainers:testcontainers-junit-jupiter:2.0.5\",\n          \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n          \"result\": \"applied\",\n          \"target\": \"tests/src/org.springframework.data/spring-data-couchbase/6.1.1/build.gradle\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"image\": \"couchbase/server:community-7.6.2\",\n          \"kind\": \"docker_image\",\n          \"result\": \"already_present\",\n          \"slug\": \"couchbase_server\",\n          \"target\": \"tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/resources/allowed-docker-images/Dockerfile-couchbase_server\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"deterministic_setup\": [\n        {\n          \"coordinate\": \"org.testcontainers:testcontainers-couchbase:2.0.5\",\n          \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n          \"reason\": \"Provides CouchbaseContainer to start a real Couchbase Server instance; spring-data-couchbase has no embedded/mock backend, and this repo already tracks testcontainers 2.0.5 (renamed 'testcontainers-couchbase' module) for other testcontainers artifacts.\",\n          \"scope\": \"testImplementation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"coordinate\": \"org.testcontainers:testcontainers-junit-jupiter:2.0.5\",\n          \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n          \"reason\": \"JUnit 5 @Testcontainers/@Container lifecycle support is a separate artifact from the couchbase module, not pulled transitively.\",\n          \"scope\": \"testImplementation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"image\": \"couchbase/server:community-7.6.2\",\n          \"kind\": \"docker_image\",\n          \"reason\": \"Community Edition avoids Enterprise licensing concerns in CI; no couchbase image is currently pinned under allowed-docker-images/, so a new Dockerfile-couchbase_server entry is needed. Exact tag should be re-verified against Testcontainers' documented default and a grype scan before pinning.\",\n          \"slug\": \"couchbase_server\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"input_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"issue\",\n          \"summary\": \"#9751 Support for org.springframework.data:spring-data-couchbase:6.1.1; label=library-new-request; body_chars=39\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"existing_tests\",\n          \"summary\": \"0 existing test file path(s) included\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"input_tokens_used\": 32,\n      \"issue_label\": \"library-new-request\",\n      \"issue_number\": 9751,\n      \"library\": \"org.springframework.data:spring-data-couchbase:6.1.1\",\n      \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n      \"output_tokens_used\": 21734,\n      \"risks\": [\n        \"Couchbase Server containers are heavier and slower to initialize than typical TCK Docker images (often 30-90s for cluster/bucket/index setup), which could strain the per-test 60s and overall suite-time budgets even when amortized across a shared container.\",\n        \"Exact image tag and testcontainers-couchbase/testcontainers-junit-jupiter versions need re-verification at generation time -- the 2.x 'testcontainers-' artifact rename is recent and I could not confirm current Maven Central coordinates against a live resolver in this sandbox.\",\n        \"Couchbase Server images tend to bundle many services (indexer, query, FTS, etc.), which may surface more CVEs under checkAllowedDockerImages/grype than smaller single-purpose images; Community Edition with a pinned minor version reduces but doesn't eliminate this.\",\n        \"This is the first org.springframework.data coordinate and the first Couchbase server Docker usage in this repo -- no local precedent exists to copy from beyond the Testcontainers pattern used by microcks-testcontainers.\"\n      ],\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"summary\": \"spring-data-couchbase's reachable surface (CouchbaseTemplate, repository proxies, N1QL query derivation, mapping/converters) only exercises real code paths against a live Couchbase cluster -- there is no embedded/in-memory substitute. The sibling spring-boot-data-couchbase test in this repo avoids this by testing only autoconfiguration wiring, which isn't an option for the core module itself. A Couchbase Testcontainers setup is needed, mirroring spring-data-couchbase's own upstream integration-test infrastructure.\"\n    },\n    \"local_ci_verification\": {\n      \"base_commit\": \"origin/master\",\n      \"commands\": [\n        {\n          \"command\": [\n            \"./gradlew\",\n            \"generateChangedIndexFileCoordinatesList\",\n            \"-PbaseCommit=origin/master\",\n            \"-PnewCommit=HEAD\"\n          ],\n          \"env\": {\n            \"GITHUB_OUTPUT\": \"/tmp/tmpv_7k4ao7\"\n          },\n          \"gate\": \"changed-index-coordinates\",\n          \"output_excerpt\": \"> Task :tck-build-logic:extractPluginRequests UP-TO-DATE\\n> Task :tck-build-logic:generatePluginAdapters UP-TO-DATE\\n> Task :tck-build-logic:compileJava UP-TO-DATE\\n> Task :tck-build-logic:compileGroovy UP-TO-DATE\\n> Task :tck-build-logic:compileGroovyPlugins UP-TO-DATE\\n> Task :tck-build-logic:pluginDescriptors UP-TO-DATE\\n> Task :tck-build-logic:processResources UP-TO-DATE\\n> Task :tck-build-logic:classes UP-TO-DATE\\n> Task :tck-build-logic:jar UP-TO-DATE\\n\\n> Configure project :\\nGraalVM Reachability Metadata TCK\\n---------------------------------\\n\\n> Task :generateChangedIndexFileCoordinatesList\\n\\n[Incubating] Problems report is available at: file:///home/mihailo/git/graalvm-reachability-metadata/forge/local_repositories/forge_worktrees/9751-b2d960c1/build/reports/problems