jq's status to mask a Grype failure. Reproduction: run `./gradlew checkAllowedDockerImages --baseCommit=origin/master --newCommit=HEAD` for a change adding an allowed image while Grype cannot load its database or catalog the image. In the recorded org.springframework.data:spring-data-couchbase:6.1.1 gate, Grype reported a stale/unloadable database and `failed to catalog` for couchbase/server:community-7.6.2, including `no space left on device`, but Gradle reported `BUILD SUCCESSFUL` and returned 0. The image therefore passed without a vulnerability scan.\"\n  }\n}\n"}
